# Data fetching

- One nested GROQ query (`sanity/lib/queries.ts` → `GUIDE_QUERY`) fetches
  the entire guide in a single request, including the `siteSettings`
  singleton. Don't split this into per-region/per-race queries —
  confirmed decision, see `docs/backend-strategy.md` §3. `getGuide()`
  returns `{regions, settings}` and is wrapped in React `cache()` so
  multiple calls on the same request share one fetch.
- Use `export const revalidate = 300` (ISR) on pages that fetch guide
  content — not `force-dynamic`, and not a webhook-triggered
  revalidation route. This is a deliberate "fewer moving parts" choice
  for volunteer/pro-bono maintenance, not an oversight.
- `useCdn: true` on the Sanity client is intentional — Studio uses
  `liveEdit` (no draft/publish copies) and Content status is the
  editorial control. There's no preview-of-unpublished-content requirement.
- `sanity/lib/client.ts` throws if `NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID` is
  missing. Keep this — fail loudly at build time rather than silently
  rendering an empty guide.
- This app has no local schema and no `sanity` package dependency — the
  Studio (and schema) live in the sibling `studio-la-forward-voter-guide`
  repo. Don't re-add `sanity.config.ts` or `schemaTypes/` here.
- `lib/types.ts` hand-mirrors `GUIDE_QUERY`'s shape (typegen deferred,
  see `docs/backend-strategy.md`). If the Studio schema changes, update
  these types by hand to match.
- `app/api/match-ballot/route.ts` is the one deliberate exception to
  "fully static/ISR, no server logic" — it geocodes an address server-side
  (Census Geocoder has no CORS support, so it can't be called from the
  browser) and returns a district match. It does not query Sanity; it
  filters the `GuideRegion[]` the client already fetched via
  `GUIDE_QUERY`. Never log the request body or the address in any catch
  block in this route — see `docs/address-matching-strategy.md`.
